# MARLEY reaction input file for neutrino CC on 40Ar
# Prepared 23 July 2018 by Steven Gardiner
#
# Particle IDs conform to the 2017 revision of the
# Particle Data Group Monte Carlo Particle Numbering Scheme
# (see http://pdg.lbl.gov/2018/reviews/rpp2018-rev-monte-carlo-numbering.pdf)
#
# B(GT) values for levels below 7.0 MeV were taken from W.
# Liu, et al., Phys. Rev. C 58, 2677 (1998). 40K excitation energies
# in this energy range were assigned using known levels tabulated in J. Chen,
# Nucl. Data Sheets 140, 1 (2017). That publication corresponds to the February
# 2017 revision of ENSDF (https://www.nndc.bnl.gov/ensdf/) for A = 40.
#
# B(GT) values for levels above 7 MeV are theoretical estimates from a QRPA
# calculation reported in M. Cheoun, et al., Eur. Phys. J. A 48, 137 (2012) and
# obtained for use with MARLEY via a private communication. The definition of
# B(GT) used in the QRPA calculation did not include the weak axial-vector
# coupling g_A, which was taken to be g_A = 1.23 by the authors when computing
# neutrino cross sections. Therefore, the QRPA B(GT) strengths taken from that
# paper were multiplied by a factor of g_A^2 = (1.23)^2 before being included
# in this file.
#
# The threshold for using theoretical B(GT) values was determined by choosing
# the first level from the QRPA calculation for which the QRPA integrated
# B(GT) strength exceeded the experimental integrated B(GT) strength at the
# highest measured experimental level.
#
# ProcessType code and nuclear target PDG code
0 1000180400 0
# Experimental Ex, B(GT) pairs taken from
# W. Liu, et al., Phys. Rev. C 58, 2677 (1998)
2.289868 0.83              1
